 "documents": {
  "plans/2026-09-20-forecast-widget.md": "# A home-screen widget for tomorrow's forecast\n\n- **Date:** 2026-09-20\n- **Slug:** forecast-widget\n- **Status:** draft\n- **Surfaces:** ios | widget\n- **Stages:** bc-implementer | bc-verifier | bc-bug-auditor\n- **Area:** universal\n\n## What this does\n\nA small home-screen widget shows tomorrow's high, low and chance of rain, so\nnobody has to open the app to decide on a jacket. It reads the forecast the\napp already keeps and refreshes when the app does.\n\n## How I'll build it\n\n1. Share the last forecast with the widget through the app group.\n2. Draw tomorrow's high, low and rain chance in the small and medium sizes.\n3. Refresh the widget whenever the app fetches a new forecast.\n\n## Files to change\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `Widget/TomorrowWidget.swift` | New widget with small and medium layouts. |\n| `App/ForecastStore.swift` | Write the last forecast into the app group. |\n| `App/Refresh.swift` | Ask the widget to reload after a fetch. |\n| `Tests/TomorrowWidgetTests.swift` | Layout and data tests for both sizes. |\n"
 }
